# playpick cell: mode=raid boss=whisper spec=paladin:holy style=idle
# size=10 difficulty=normal view=390x844,touch save=fresh
#
# What no session has done before: every prior idle-style reading of The
# Last Whisper's shade mark (2026-09-27-17, warrior:protection) came from a
# tank, and the two pulls that actually landed shade hits on a stationary
# body (2026-09-27-20 auto-warlock, 2026-09-28-7 mash-druid:restoration)
# were both at 25-heroic inside an evening, and neither style is a body that
# truly never acts -- auto and mash both still press abilities, just without
# steering. idle never casts and never moves at all, so a healer under idle
# is the first body on this exact boss with nothing to answer shade with
# even if it lands: no self-heal, no movement to break the mark's chase.
# This is also the first direct mode=raid idle-healer pull of this specific
# boss at its easiest setting (10-normal), matching the tank pull's own cell
# so the two are a controlled pair on role alone.
open #b=whisper&s=10&h=0
targets
tap class:paladin:holy
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

play idle 80
state
shot mid1
bill

play idle 80
state
shot mid2
bill

play idle 80
state
shot end
says
bill
